      "content": "That's much better. The technical depth in the Methodology and Statistical sections is exactly what I was looking for. \n\nI noticed it cut off at the end there though, so please finish the thought regarding the disconnect between claims and evidence. \n\nAlso, looking at the draft, I think we can make it even more organized for the editorial board. It would be helpful to have the review broken down into a more granular, modular format. Try to use a more comprehensive structure with several distinct sections and sub-headings for every individual point of criticism. This will help the editors navigate the specific technical failures one by one. \n\nJust a reminder: please ensure each section is actually substantive and doesn't just repeat what was said elsewhere. I'm looking for high-quality, granular detail, not just a bunch of empty headers. Keep the focus on the rigor.",
